1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,151
Book Two, Proposition Seven.

2
00:00:02,151 --> 00:00:15,693
If a segment be cut at random, the square on the whole and that on one of the segments both together are equal to twice the rectangle contained by the whole and the said segment, and the square on the remaining segment.

3
00:00:15,693 --> 00:00:18,290
Let the segment A B be cut at random at C.

4
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:25,897
On A B, describe the square A D E B by One Forty-Six, and draw the diagonal B D.

5
00:00:25,897 --> 00:00:35,600
Complete the figure by drawing C N parallel to A D or B E, and through G drawing H F parallel to A B or D E.

6
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:40,723
By One Forty-Three, the complement A G equals the complement G E.

7
00:00:40,723 --> 00:00:49,983
Add the square C F to each; then the whole rectangle A F equals the whole rectangle C E, so A F and C E together are double A F.

8
00:00:49,983 --> 00:00:55,698
Yet A F and C E together form the gnomon K L M plus the overlapping square C F.

9
00:00:55,698 --> 00:01:06,984
And because B F equals B C, A F is the rectangle contained by A B and B C; therefore the gnomon K L M and the square C F equal twice the rectangle A B, B C.

10
00:01:06,984 --> 00:01:10,529
Add D G, which equals the square on A C, to each.

11
00:01:10,529 --> 00:01:17,330
The gnomon K L M and D G form the whole square A D E B on A B, while C F is the square on B C.

12
00:01:17,330 --> 00:01:26,156
Therefore, the squares on A B and B C equal twice the rectangle contained by A B and B C, together with the square on A C.

13
00:01:26,156 --> 00:01:27,820
Which was to be proved.

14
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:33,190
Proposition Two Seven is the geometric counterpart to the square of a difference.

15
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:48,348
Calling the whole line a and the segment b, their difference is a minus b, and the diagram shows that a squared plus b squared equals two a b plus the square on a minus b—because the two full rectangles A F and C E overlap on the corner square C F.

16
00:01:48,348 --> 00:02:02,160
